summary:
- topic: Superintendent Search Update
  text: The South Portland Board of Education announced that a preferred candidate
    for Superintendent has been identified, and the Chair was authorized to enter
    into negotiations. Further details will be released once discussions are complete.
- topic: Student Representative Recognition
  text: Graduating student representatives, Alex Davison and Angela Kabisa, were honored
    for their dedicated service and valuable insights to the Board during their tenure.
    Board members praised their maturity and contributions during challenging times.
- topic: South Portland High School Top Scholars 2026
  text: The Board celebrated the South Portland High School Top Scholars for 2026,
    with each student receiving a certificate and introducing a peer, highlighting
    their academic achievements, extracurricular involvement, and future plans.
- topic: FY26-27 Budget and Audit Update
  text: The Finance Committee reported on the FY26-27 budget development, noting a
    reduced deficit range and ongoing efforts to implement payroll encumbrances for
    more accurate projections. The Director of Finance also provided an update on
    the FY25 audit, emphasizing a multi-year effort to improve internal processes
    and reconciliation procedures.
- topic: Elementary Reconfiguration and Kaler Student Placement
  text: An update was provided on the Elementary Reconfiguration Steering Committee,
    which includes 23 members. The principal of Kaler Elementary School discussed
    the complexities of placing Kaler students due to uncertain future reconfiguration
    structures and mentioned a parent survey to gather feedback on placement preferences.
- topic: MaineCare Billing Practices
  text: The Director of Instructional Support presented an overview of MaineCare billing
    for school services, explaining the need for parental consent and the risks of
    audits. Potential areas for increased billing, such as day treatment and psychological
    evaluations, were discussed alongside associated regulatory and staffing challenges.
- topic: Student Transportation Safety Concerns
  text: Public comments from parents and staff raised serious safety concerns regarding
    overcrowded buses for athletic events and daily school routes, with students reportedly
    standing in aisles and sitting on laps. The Superintendent committed to investigating
    these issues and providing a report at the next meeting.
- topic: Policy First Reads
  text: 'The Board conducted first reads for Policy BEDB: Agenda, which outlines agenda
    procedures, and the Educational Equity Policy, which aims to ensure equitable
    practices across the district. Discussions included the importance of accessible
    data for equity reviews.'
